-- NEGATIVE fixture for the future D-CYCLE check, and THE THREE-GRAPH WITNESS of
-- the set (spec §6.4.2, §6.3.7, §6.3.10).
--
-- p6: mutual recursion between two nullary decides that live in DIFFERENT `§`
-- sections.
--
--     § part one : `the part one figure` reads `the part two figure`
--     § part two : `the part two figure` reads `the part one figure`
--
-- It is the only fixture in the set that lands in all three graphs at once:
--   * the decision graph            -> §6.3.7 D-CYCLE, today;
--   * the knowledgeRequirement graph -> §6.3.9, once the members un-lift;
--   * the decisionService graph      -> §6.3.10, once a `§` becomes a service.
--
-- PAIR IT WITH THE RUNTIME PROBE. jl4/tests-cli/fixtures/dmn-bkm-probe/
-- svc-cycle.dmn is the same hazard expressed directly in DMN, and its measured
-- verdict is: Xerces VALID, KIE validator CLEAN, KIE runtime answers null while
-- reporting the decisions SUCCEEDED (it does also emit runtime ERROR messages,
-- which a design-time exporter cannot see). So no engine catches this at build
-- time. The only detector that can is ours, which is why this fixture is not
-- decorative.
--
-- On today's tree the emitted DRG IS cyclic here and the report is ADVISORY
-- ONLY.
--
-- Expected after Phase 4: one D-CYCLE over an SCC of size 2 spanning two
-- sections, at Blocking rather than advisory severity.
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `part one`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part one figure` MEANS
    `the part two figure` PLUS 1

§ `part two`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part two figure` MEANS
    `the part one figure` PLUS 1
